  "insights": [
   "Hyperscalers are increasingly utilizing finance leases for data center shells to accelerate capacity expansion, manage liquidity, and secure optionality.",
   "Up to 20% of the projected $2tn in hyperscaler capital investment over the next 3 years is expected to be funded via data center shell finance leases.",
   "Hyperscalers have disclosed $388bn in signed but uncommenced lease commitments, indicating a massive pipeline of future capital outlays.",
   "Accounting for these leases is highly discretionary, with significant variation in how companies classify leases (finance vs. operating) and present them in free cash flow (FCF) metrics.",
   "Finance leases effectively function as debt-financed asset purchases, transferring risks and rewards to the tenant, yet they are often excluded from standard capex and FCF calculations.",
   "Investors should adjust FCF to include finance lease principal payments to better evaluate cash available for dividends and buybacks, and include total asset acquisitions for apples-to-apples capex comparisons.",
   "Management judgment regarding lease terms, renewal options, and residual value guarantees creates meaningful accounting divergence across the sector.",
   "The report provides an illustrative case study of Oracle's (ORCL) Stargate project, estimating a $15bn lease liability for the Abilene Phase 2 site."
